      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From my testing it seems Unity 6 will retain it's maximized status between restarts if you maximize it at **any** point (even if you un-maximize it before closing the game).\n\nI normally run the game with these launch args:\n\n-screen-width 1920 -screen-height 1080  --enforce-world-server-checks --enable-debug-gui --fps=60  --enable-udon-debug-logging --enable-sdk-log-levels\n\nHowever I found out if you define the monitor with -monitor and have -screen-fullscreen as 0 it'll work as expected and not maximize the game.\n\n-monitor 0 -screen-fullscreen 0 -screen-width 1920 -screen-height 1080  --enforce-world-server-checks --enable-debug-gui --fps=60  --enable-udon-debug-logging --enable-sdk-log-levels",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
